  texts:
  - key: PIO.01.01
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Pioneer quer dizer pioneira: quem vai primeiro. E o nome n\xE3o \xE9 por acaso."
    enText: 'Pioneer: a word for those who go first. And the name was no accident.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.01.02
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Mar\xE7o de 1972. Uma pequena sonda, do tamanho de um carro, partiu rumo aos planetas exteriores."
    enText: March 1972. No machine of ours had ever travelled beyond Mars. This small probe, no bigger than a car, was about to try.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.01.03
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Onze horas depois de deixar o ch\xE3o, passou pela Lua."
    enText: Eleven hours after leaving the ground, it swept past the Moon.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.01.04
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Ela gira devagar, como um pi\xE3o. Esse giro ajuda a manter a sonda est\xE1vel na longa viagem."
    enText: It spins slowly, like a top, and that steady turning keeps it upright and pointed home towards Earth.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.01.05
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Longe do Sol, a luz \xE9 fraca demais, ent\xE3o a Pioneer fazia a pr\xF3pria energia com geradores RTG."
    enText: But far from the Sun, sunlight is too faint, so Pioneer made its own power with RTG generators.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.01.06
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Nada feito por m\xE3os humanas tinha viajado t\xE3o depressa."
    enText: Nothing built by human hands had ever travelled so fast.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.02.01
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Depois de Marte, havia um lugar onde ningu\xE9m tinha passado: o cintur\xE3o de asteroides."
    enText: 'Mars fell behind. Ahead lay a place no one had ever crossed: the asteroid belt.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.02.02
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Ningu\xE9m sabia quantas pedras havia. Ningu\xE9m sabia se dava para atravessar."
    enText: Nobody knew how many rocks lay in wait. Nobody knew whether anything could pass through at all.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.02.03
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Alguns cientistas temiam que uma \xFAnica colis\xE3o encerrasse a miss\xE3o."
    enText: Some scientists feared that a single collision would end the mission.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.02.04
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Na vida real, as pedras ficam muito longe umas das outras. A rota passava a milh\xF5es de km da mais pr\xF3xima."
    enText: 'And then, a surprise: the rocks lay vast distances apart, and the route passed millions of kilometres from the nearest known asteroid.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.02.05
    group: narrative
    ptText: "S\xF3 poeira fina ro\xE7ou a sonda."
    enText: Only fine dust brushed against the probe.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.02.06
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Sete meses depois, a Pioneer saiu do outro lado, inteira. D\xE1 para atravessar o cintur\xE3o!"
    enText: After seven months, Pioneer emerged on the far side, unharmed. The belt could be crossed.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.02.07
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Ent\xE3o os dias foram contados: uma semana, um m\xEAs, e depois meses passando cada vez mais depressa."
    enText: So the days were counted. A week. A month. Then months, slipping by faster and faster.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.03.01
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Novembro de 1973. J\xFApiter, o maior dos planetas, j\xE1 estava \xE0 vista."
    enText: Which left the greatest prize of all. By November 1973, Jupiter, largest of the planets, was in sight.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.03.02
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Um mundo t\xE3o grande que onze Terras caberiam lado a lado em seu di\xE2metro."
    enText: A world so vast that eleven Earths could stand side by side across its face.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.03.03
    group: narrative
    ptText: "A Pioneer come\xE7ou a fotografar de longe, a 25 milh\xF5es de quil\xF4metros."
    enText: Pioneer began taking pictures from 25 million kilometres away.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.03.04
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Mas um comando e sua resposta podiam levar at\xE9 uma hora e meia."
    enText: Yet a command and its reply could take up to an hour and a half.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.04.01
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Mas a Pioneer n\xE3o tinha uma c\xE2mera como a do seu celular."
    enText: Yet Pioneer had no camera like the one in your phone.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.04.02
    group: narrative
    ptText: "A cada volta, via s\xF3 uma linha fina de J\xFApiter, em duas cores: vermelho e azul."
    enText: 'With each turn, it saw just one thin line of Jupiter, in only two colours: red and blue.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.04.03
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Vermelho e azul eram medidos juntos, mas uma foto sozinha vinha cheia de ru\xEDdo."
    enText: Red and blue were measured together, but a single photo came out full of noise.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.04.04
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Somando v\xE1rias fotos, o ru\xEDdo some e a imagem aparece."
    enText: Adding photos together, the noise fades and the picture appears.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.04.05
    group: narrative
    ptText: Vermelho e azul vieram do instrumento. A terceira cor teria de ser calculada na Terra.
    enText: Red and blue came from the instrument. The third colour would be worked out on Earth.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.04.06
    group: narrative
    ptText: "A Pioneer nunca viu o verde. Os computadores na Terra o estimaram, e J\xFApiter apareceu em cores."
    enText: Pioneer never saw green. Computers on Earth worked it out, and Jupiter appeared in colour.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.04.07
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Fotografia real, 1973: J\xFApiter como a Pioneer 10 o registrou."
    enText: 'Real photograph, 1973: Jupiter as Pioneer 10 recorded it.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.04.08
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Foi a primeira nave a fazer fotos de perto de J\xFApiter."
    enText: It was the first spacecraft to take close-up pictures of Jupiter.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.04.09
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Eram imagens melhores que qualquer telesc\xF3pio da Terra podia oferecer."
    enText: These pictures were sharper than anything a telescope on Earth could offer.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.09.01
    group: narrative
    ptText: Cada vez mais perto, passou pelas grandes luas e fez as primeiras fotos de perto de Ganimedes, a maior lua do Sistema Solar.
    enText: Closer it came, passing Jupiter's great moons and taking the first close-up pictures of Ganymede, the largest moon in the Solar System.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.09.02
    group: narrative
    ptText: "J\xFApiter \xE9 cercado por radia\xE7\xE3o milhares de vezes mais forte que a da Terra."
    enText: For Jupiter is wrapped in radiation thousands of times stronger than anything near Earth.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.09.03
    group: narrative
    ptText: Absorveu mais de mil vezes a dose fatal a uma pessoa. Surgiram comandos indevidos; havia reservas.
    enText: Pioneer absorbed more than a thousand times the dose that would be fatal to a person.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.09.04
    group: narrative
    ptText: "4 de dezembro de 1973: a Pioneer 10 foi a primeira a sobrevoar J\xFApiter."
    enText: Closest approach. Pioneer 10 became the first probe ever to visit Jupiter.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.09.05
    group: narrative
    ptText: "A cerca de 130.000 km das nuvens: tr\xEAs vezes mais perto que a Lua da Terra."
    enText: 'It passed about 130,000 kilometres above the clouds: three times closer than the Moon is to us.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.09.06
    group: narrative
    ptText: "A gravidade de J\xFApiter curvou seu caminho e deu o impulso para seguir al\xE9m dos planetas."
    enText: "Jupiter\u2019s gravity bent its path and gave it the boost to travel beyond the planets."
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.09.07
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Viu que a radia\xE7\xE3o de J\xFApiter era mais forte que o esperado, e isso mudou a Voyager."
    enText: "It found Jupiter\u2019s radiation fiercer than expected, which shaped Voyager\u2019s design."
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.09.08
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Fotografou tamb\xE9m Calisto e Europa, mas s\xF3 em baixa resolu\xE7\xE3o."
    enText: It also photographed Callisto and Europa, though only in low resolution.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.09.09
    group: narrative
    ptText: "J\xFApiter corre ao redor do Sol e a Pioneer pegou carona nessa velocidade."
    enText: Jupiter is itself racing around the Sun, and the probe borrowed a little of that speed, rather like hitching a lift.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.09.10
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Uma imagem de Io foi feita, mas a radia\xE7\xE3o a destruiu."
    enText: An image of Io was taken too, but it was lost to the radiation.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.05.01
    group: narrative
    ptText: "J\xFApiter ficou para tr\xE1s. N\xE3o haveria volta: a Pioneer seguia para as estrelas."
    enText: 'Then Jupiter fell behind. There would be no return journey: Pioneer was bound for the stars.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.05.02
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Hidrog\xEAnio, o \xE1tomo mais comum do Universo: a nossa r\xE9gua."
    enText: 'First, hydrogen, the commonest atom in the Universe: our ruler.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.05.03
    group: narrative
    ptText: 'Pulsares: estrelas que piscam e mostram onde fica o Sol.'
    enText: Then a map of blinking stars, called pulsars, to show where the Sun lies.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.05.04
    group: narrative
    ptText: 'O Sistema Solar: a sonda saindo do terceiro planeta, a Terra.'
    enText: 'The Solar System follows, with Pioneer leaving the third planet: Earth.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.05.05
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Ao lado, o contorno da pr\xF3pria Pioneer, para dar escala."
    enText: Beside it, the outline of Pioneer itself, so that our size can be judged.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.05.06
    group: narrative
    ptText: "E duas figuras. Uma delas acena: ol\xE1!"
    enText: And before it, two figures. One of them is waving hello.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.05.07
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Uma placa de alum\xEDnio dourado: uma carta para um encontro que talvez nunca aconte\xE7a."
    enText: 'A gold-coloured aluminium plaque: a letter for an encounter that may never happen.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.06.01
    group: narrative
    ptText: A Pioneer foi feita para durar vinte e um meses. Simplesmente continuou.
    enText: Pioneer had been built to last twenty-one months. It simply carried on.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.06.02
    group: narrative
    ptText: "13 de junho de 1983: cruzou a dist\xE2ncia da \xF3rbita de Netuno, com os instrumentos ainda funcionando normalmente."
    enText: "13 June 1983: it crossed the distance of Neptune\u2019s orbit, its instruments still working normally."
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.06.03
    group: narrative
    ptText: "1989: a energia diminu\xEDa. Os instrumentos passaram a se revezar, e o computador de comandos foi desligado."
    enText: '1989: its power was fading. The instruments now took turns, and the command computer was switched off.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.06.04
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Em 1998, a Voyager 1 a ultrapassou e se tornou a m\xE1quina humana mais distante, em outra dire\xE7\xE3o."
    enText: In 1998, Voyager 1 overtook it to become the most distant human-made object. Pioneer had shown the way.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.06.05
    group: narrative
    ptText: A Pioneer havia mostrado o caminho. Agora, a Terra escutava cada vez mais longe.
    enText: Pioneer had shown the way. Now Earth had to listen from ever farther away.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.06.06
    group: narrative
    ptText: "1993: para poupar energia, a c\xE2mera que fotografou J\xFApiter foi desligada, e depois o detector de radia\xE7\xE3o."
    enText: '1993: to save power, the camera that had photographed Jupiter was switched off, followed by the radiation detector.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.07.01
    group: narrative
    ptText: O sinal estava mais fraco que um sussurro. As antenas da Terra ainda conseguiriam ouvi-lo?
    enText: Its signal was now fainter than a whisper. Could Earth still hear it?
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.07.02
    group: narrative
    ptText: Conseguiu. Trinta anos depois, a Pioneer ainda respondia.
    enText: It could. Thirty years on, Pioneer was still answering.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.07.03
    group: narrative
    ptText: "27 de abril de 2002: chegaram os \xFAltimos dados."
    enText: '27 April 2002: the last data arrived.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.07.04
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Janeiro de 2003. Um \xFAltimo sinal fraco, de 12 bilh\xF5es de quil\xF4metros, levou mais de 11 horas para chegar."
    enText: '23 January 2003: a final signal, from twelve billion kilometres away, taking over eleven hours to reach us.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.07.05
    group: narrative
    ptText: Fevereiro de 2003. A Terra escutou outra vez e nenhum sinal foi detectado.
    enText: '7 February 2003: Earth listened once more, and heard nothing.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.07.06
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Sem energia suficiente para nos alcan\xE7ar, a Pioneer 10 ficou em sil\xEAncio. Mas n\xE3o parou."
    enText: Its power had finally run out, and Pioneer 10 fell silent. But it did not stop.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.08.01
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Ela segue em dire\xE7\xE3o \xE0 estrela vermelha Aldebaran: uma viagem de milh\xF5es de anos."
    enText: 'It travels on, towards the red star Aldebaran: a journey of some two million years.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.08.02
    group: narrative
    ptText: Feita para durar 21 meses, funcionou por mais de 30 anos.
    enText: Built to last twenty-one months, it lasted more than thirty years.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.08.03
    group: narrative
    ptText: "E o nome n\xE3o foi por acaso. Veja o que ela fez primeiro."
    enText: And the name was no accident. Look at what it did first.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.08.04
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Pioneer quer dizer pioneira. Toda grande viagem come\xE7a com quem vai primeiro, e a Pioneer 10 foi primeiro, por todos n\xF3s."
    enText: 'Pioneer: one who goes first. Every great journey begins with someone willing to go first. Pioneer 10 went first, for all of us.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.UI.start
    group: hud
    ptText: "Pioneer 10 \xB7 Abrir caminho"
    enText: "Pioneer 10 \xB7 Going first"
    ptStatus: approved
    enStatus: approved
